{{! /freestyle/tricks — trick dictionary index }}

<div class="hero hero-sm">
  <div>
    {{#if navigation.breadcrumbs}}
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      {{#each navigation.breadcrumbs}}
        {{#if href}}<a href="{{href}}">{{label}}</a> <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span> {{else}}<span>{{label}}</span>{{/if}}
      {{/each}}
    </nav>
    {{/if}}
    <h1>{{page.title}}</h1>
    {{#if page.intro}}<p class="hero-subtitle">{{page.intro}}</p>{{/if}}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrapper">

  {{! ── Dictionary size, visible before any browsing choice: the unfiltered
      total, the filtered M-of-N, or the ADD tier's own count. ── }}
  <p class="dict-header-count">{{content.headerCount}}</p>

  {{! ── Actions card: the two things a reader can DO from here, on one row.
      Search submits to the dedicated search page (typeahead lives there) and
      works without JS; Watch Videos leaves for the freestyle media hub, so it
      is a button, not a tile that looks like it would open in place. ── }}
  <div class="card search-box-card mt-5" id="dictionary-top">
    <div class="search-box-section">
      <h2 class="card-title">{{content.searchSection.heading}}</h2>
      <form method="GET" action="/freestyle/search" class="search-box-form" role="search">
        <input type="text" name="q" minlength="2" maxlength="100"
               placeholder="Name or alias"
               aria-label="Search tricks by name or alias"
               title="Search tricks by name or alias"
               autocomplete="off"
               class="search-box-input" />
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Search</button>
      </form>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="{{content.watchVideosButton.href}}">{{content.watchVideosButton.label}}</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  {{! ── Reading the Dictionary: platform-ontology orientation, folded closed
      above the browse controls on every view. Explains the trick-row
      contract, the browse views, and the kinds of object the platform
      deliberately keeps separate. Foundational orientation only; do NOT
      harden family-hierarchy language here, the family taxonomy framing is
      curator-owned. Deep links land on the <details> id; the inner section
      keeps its own id so both anchor forms resolve. }}
  <div class="dict-tile-grid" aria-label="Reading the Dictionary">
  <details class="dict-tile" id="reading-the-dictionary">
    <summary class="dict-tile-summary">
      <h2 class="dict-tile-title">Reading the Dictionary</h2>
      <span class="dict-tile-hint">How the dictionary describes every trick and the kinds of object it keeps separate.</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="dict-tile-body">
  <section class="content-section" id="section-reading-the-dictionary">
    <p>
      Three things about how the dictionary
      presents tricks: the <strong>row</strong> every trick shares, the
      <strong>browse views</strong> that regroup those rows, and the six
      <strong>kinds of object</strong> the platform keeps separate, where
      older footbag vocabularies often used one flat name for all of them.
    </p>

    <h3 class="section-heading">The trick row</h3>
    <p class="detail-muted">Every documented trick uses the same two-line row in the browse views; only the grouping around it changes.</p>
    <div class="glossary-row-contract">
      <p class="glossary-row-contract-line"><span class="glossary-row-contract-label">Line 1</span> canonical trick name &middot; <code>#hashtag</code> &middot; optional <strong>&equiv;</strong> interpretation / decomposition reading &middot; a <a href="/freestyle/concepts#section-media-claim-scope">Media</a> link when the trick has clips</p>
      <p class="glossary-row-contract-line"><span class="glossary-row-contract-label">Line 2</span> <strong>JOB</strong> operational notation &middot; <strong>ADD</strong> component accounting (the traditional additive score; not a direct measure of execution difficulty)</p>
    </div>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      There is no separate per-row ADD chip. In <strong>By ADD</strong>, the
      section heading supplies the ADD total and the line-2
      <strong>ADD</strong> expression shows how that total is accounted for; in
      the other browse views, the same ADD expression remains part of the trick
      row. JOB (<a href="/freestyle/concepts#section-notation">notation</a>) and ADD
      (<a href="/freestyle/concepts#section-add-accounting">accounting</a>) are the two halves of
      line 2; both are explained in full in Freestyle Concepts.
    </p>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      Two cautions about line 1. An <strong>alias</strong> (a second name for the
      same trick, e.g. catwalk = eclipse) is <em>not</em> an interpretation;
      it is the same trick under another name, with no
      <strong>&equiv;</strong> reading implied. And an interpretation is
      <em>not always settled doctrine</em>: some <strong>&equiv;</strong> readings
      are ratified structure, others are observational or depend on a curator
      ruling and may change. The <strong>&equiv;</strong> shows the reading; it
      does not promise the reading is final.
    </p>

    <h3 class="section-heading">The browse views</h3>
    <p class="detail-muted">Same rows, seven lenses. Each answers a different question. By ADD, By family, By set, and By modifier are the main views; the other three sit behind the <strong>Other views</strong> control below.</p>
    <div class="glossary-add-weight-table-wrap">
      <table class="glossary-add-weight-table">
        <thead><tr><th>View</th><th>Groups by</th><th>Reveals</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><a href="/freestyle/tricks?view=add">By ADD</a></td><td>ADD total</td><td>how the scoring system counts the trick&rsquo;s components</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="/freestyle/tricks?view=family">By family</a></td><td>conserved terminal mechanic</td><td>structural lineage</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="/freestyle/tricks?view=set">By set</a></td><td>the named launch set the trick opens with</td><td>how tricks begin</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="/freestyle/tricks?view=modifier">By modifier</a></td><td>the body or timing modifier used</td><td>what transforms the base</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="/freestyle/tricks?view=movement-system">By movement system</a></td><td>four conceptual axes (+ alternative surfaces)</td><td>the compositional system</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="/freestyle/tricks?view=topology">Movement Neighborhoods</a></td><td>&ldquo;feels mechanically similar&rdquo;</td><td>exploratory similarity, not a canonical taxonomy</td></tr>
          <tr><td><a href="/freestyle/tricks?view=dex-count">By dex count</a></td><td>number of <a href="/freestyle/concepts#section-dexterities">dex</a> events</td><td>mechanical complexity</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      Tricks with the same ADD total are not necessarily equally difficult to
      perform; ADD counts recognized components rather than every factor that
      affects execution difficulty.
    </p>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      A trick may appear in several of these views at once. Each lens asks a
      different question about the same trick.
    </p>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      The Family, Set, and Modifier views are <strong>curated for useful
      browsing</strong>, not for listing every taxonomic term. Each shows the
      groupings worth browsing and explains its choices in a small
      &ldquo;Why these groups?&rdquo; note on the page. For everything beyond
      the browse groupings, two reference surfaces go deeper: the
      <a href="/freestyle/sets">Set Encyclopedia</a> covers the full set
      vocabulary, and the <a href="/freestyle/operators">Operators &amp;
      Modifiers reference</a> covers the broader modifier and operator
      vocabulary.
    </p>

    <h3 class="section-heading">Six kinds of object (and why they stay separate)</h3>
    <p>
      Older footbag vocabularies flattened families, modifiers, surfaces,
      aliases, and decompositions into one undifferentiated name-space. The
      platform keeps them separate because each is a <em>different kind of
      thing</em>, governed by different rules; conflating them is what
      makes a flat vocabulary confusing.
    </p>
    <div class="glossary-add-weight-table-wrap">
      <table class="glossary-add-weight-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>What it is</th><th>Example</th><th>Where it lives</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Canonical family</td><td>a true structural lineage sharing a conserved terminal mechanic</td><td>whirl, mirage, legover</td><td>By family</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Set / set system</td><td>a named launch or entry structure that opens a trick</td><td>pixie, stepping, atomic</td><td>By set; the <a href="/freestyle/sets">Set Encyclopedia</a> goes deeper</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Modifier / operator</td><td>a movement idea applied to a base; transforms many bases, with no terminal mechanic of its own</td><td>paradox, symposium, spinning, ducking</td><td>By modifier; <a href="/freestyle/operators">Operators &amp; Modifiers</a> goes deeper</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Alternative surface</td><td>an unusual catch surface, not a movement lineage</td><td>sole, heel, cloud, cross-body sole</td><td>Movement system &rarr; Alternative surfaces</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Movement neighborhood</td><td>tricks that <em>feel</em> mechanically similar (an exploratory lens, not a taxonomy)</td><td>Hippy downtime dex</td><td>Movement Neighborhoods</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Alias / decomposition reading</td><td>another name for, or a structural reading of, an existing trick (descriptive, not a new trick)</td><td>catwalk = eclipse; eggbeater &equiv; atomic legover</td><td>(no own view; shown on the trick)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      The boundaries: a <strong>canonical family</strong> has its own terminal
      mechanic; a <strong>set</strong> is how a trick begins; a
      <strong>modifier</strong> transforms a base and has no terminal mechanic
      of its own; an <strong>alternative surface</strong> is a contact surface,
      not a lineage; a <strong>neighborhood</strong> is &ldquo;feels
      similar,&rdquo; not &ldquo;is structurally the same&rdquo;; and an
      <strong>interpretation reading</strong> (the <strong>&equiv;</strong> on
      line 1) describes an equivalence; it does not make the read-as name a
      productive modifier.
    </p>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      The <strong>family</strong> kind is not flat. A family is read on two
      independent axes: its <strong>lineage position</strong> (a root, or a branch
      of another family) and its <strong>display tier</strong> (a Family Parent, or
      a Minor Lineage below the descendant-count threshold). The
      <a href="/freestyle/concepts#section-families">Families</a> chapter of Freestyle Concepts maps both.
    </p>

    <h3 class="section-heading">Reading a compound name</h3>
    <p>
      Many compositional trick names can be read from the end. The
      <strong>final term</strong> often identifies the base trick, and with it
      the <a href="/freestyle/concepts#section-families">family</a> the trick belongs to, while
      the terms before it describe
      <a href="/freestyle/concepts#section-modifiers">structures applied</a> to that base. For
      names built this way, the ending says what the trick fundamentally is,
      and the leading words say what has been done to it.
    </p>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      Word order carries the meaning, not just the words. The same two words in
      the opposite order name two different tricks in two different families.
      These are not the same two movements performed in a different sequence:
      they are coordinated movements whose identities differ because the base
      trick differs.
    </p>
    <div class="glossary-add-weight-table-wrap">
      <table class="glossary-add-weight-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Compound name</th><th>Reads as</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/freestyle/tricks/whirling_swirl">Whirling Swirl</a></td>
            <td>a <a href="/freestyle/tricks/swirl">swirl</a> (the base), with whirling applied</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/freestyle/tricks/swirling_whirl">Swirling Whirl</a></td>
            <td>a <a href="/freestyle/tricks/whirl">whirl</a> (the base), with swirling applied</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="detail-muted">
      Reversing the words flips the base from swirl to whirl, so the family
      flips too, and a <a href="/freestyle/tricks/whirl">whirl</a> and a
      <a href="/freestyle/tricks/swirl">swirl</a> are genuinely different
      families. The pair also shows that structural identity, ADD accounting,
      and execution difficulty are three different dimensions: the two names
      carry the same ADD total, yet the movements can differ substantially in
      how hard they are to perform. Read the last word first and the rest of a
      compositional name usually falls into place.
    </p>
  </section>
    </div>
  </details>
  </div>

  {{! ── Orientation tiles: one wrapping row of three closed disclosures holding
      the beginner links, the how-tricks-are-built primer, and what the
      dictionary contains, ordered beginner to expert. Every tile in the row
      behaves the same way (opens in place, independently, nothing persists),
      so the row carries no control that navigates away. An open tile stretches
      to the full row and the rest reflow. Default landing only: secondary
      views and the family filter carry their own state-specific
      orientation. ── }}
  {{#if (eq content.activeView "add")}}
  {{#unless content.activeFamily}}
  {{#unless content.isAddTierView}}
  <div class="dict-tile-grid" aria-label="About the dictionary">
    <details class="dict-tile">
      <summary class="dict-tile-summary">
        <span class="dict-tile-title">{{content.landingTiles.start.title}}</span>
        <span class="dict-tile-hint">{{content.landingTiles.start.hint}}</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="dict-tile-body">
        {{! Each of these is a destination that must read as important without
            being a button, which is the prominent-action-link tier; as
            dot-separated prose links they read as running text instead. }}
        <div class="dict-onboarding-links">
          {{#each content.landingOnboarding.links}}<a class="action-link" href="{{href}}">{{label}}</a>{{/each}}
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="dict-tile">
      <summary class="dict-tile-summary">
        <span class="dict-tile-title">{{content.landingTiles.built.title}}</span>
        <span class="dict-tile-hint">{{content.landingTiles.built.hint}}</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="dict-tile-body">
        {{#each content.landingOnboarding.intro}}<p class="dict-onboarding-intro">{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
        {{#if content.landingOnboarding.definitions.length}}
        <dl class="dict-onboarding-defs">
          {{#each content.landingOnboarding.definitions}}<div class="dict-onboarding-def"><dt>{{term}}</dt><dd>{{plain}}</dd></div>{{/each}}
        </dl>
        {{/if}}
        <p class="dict-onboarding-example">
          <span class="dict-onboarding-example-label">{{content.landingOnboarding.example.label}}:</span>
          {{#each content.landingOnboarding.example.steps}}<span class="dict-onboarding-step"><strong>{{name}}</strong> <span class="dict-onboarding-step-note">{{note}}</span></span>{{#unless @last}} <span class="dict-onboarding-arrow">&rarr;</span> {{/unless}}{{/each}}
        </p>
        <ul class="dict-onboarding-lenses">
          {{#each content.landingOnboarding.lenses}}<li><strong>{{label}}</strong> <span class="dict-onboarding-lens-note">{{note}}</span></li>{{/each}}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="dict-tile">
      <summary class="dict-tile-summary">
        <span class="dict-tile-title">{{content.landingTiles.contents.title}}</span>
        <span class="dict-tile-hint">{{content.landingTiles.contents.hint}}</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="dict-tile-body">
        {{#if content.dictionaryStats}}
        <p class="browse-view-scale">{{content.dictionaryStats}}</p>
        {{/if}}
        {{! Where the data comes from belongs with what is in the dictionary,
            up here where a reader meets it, not stranded under the list. }}
        <p class="source-note">
          Trick data sourced from community documentation.
          ADD values follow the traditional additive component-accounting system;
          see <a href="/freestyle/add-analysis">ADD Accounting &amp; Analysis</a> for
          a step-by-step walkthrough of how totals are constructed, with worked
          examples and discrepancy case studies.
          Tricks with documented records are linked to their record pages.
        </p>
        <p class="dict-emerging-line"><a href="{{content.emergingLine.titleHref}}">{{content.emergingLine.titleLabel}}</a>: {{content.emergingLine.sentence}}</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
  {{/unless}}
  {{/unless}}
  {{/if}}

  {{#if content.activeFamily}}
  <p class="browse-view-intro">{{content.familyFilterIntro}}
    <a class="dictionary-intro-glossary-link" href="#reading-the-dictionary">New to the dictionary? Read "Reading the Dictionary" above</a>
    &nbsp;<a href="/freestyle/tricks">Clear the filter</a> to see the full dictionary.</p>
  {{#if content.relatedModifierGroups.length}}
  <nav class="related-modifier-groups" aria-label="Related set or modifier groups">
    <span class="related-modifier-groups-label">Related set/modifier groups:</span>
    {{#each content.relatedModifierGroups}}
      <a class="related-modifier-group-link" href="{{{href}}}">{{modifierName}} <span class="related-modifier-group-count">({{count}})</span></a>{{#unless @last}} <span class="related-modifier-group-sep">·</span> {{/unless}}
    {{/each}}
  </nav>
  {{/if}}
  {{/if}}

  {{! ── Browse navigation, gathered into one titled card so the three control
      rows (which view, how each tier sorts, and where to jump) read as one
      thing rather than three loose lines. "By ADD" is the default; the other
      systems are secondary ways to navigate the same movement universe. No
      JavaScript; view selected via the ?view= query param. ── }}
  <div class="card dict-nav-card">
    <h2 class="card-title">{{content.navSection.heading}}</h2>
  {{! Each entry carries the lens question as its title, so what an axis is FOR
      arrives on hover and focus instead of costing a line of layout. }}
  <nav class="trick-view-toggle" aria-label="Browse the dictionary">
    <span class="dict-nav-label">{{content.navSection.viewLabel}}</span>
    {{#if (eq content.activeView "add")}}
      <span title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.add}}" class="trick-view-toggle-active">By ADD</span>
    {{else}}
      <a title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.add}}" href="/freestyle/tricks?view=add">By ADD</a>
    {{/if}}
    <span class="trick-view-toggle-sep">·</span>
    {{#if (eq content.activeView "family")}}
      <span title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.family}}" class="trick-view-toggle-active">By family</span>
    {{else}}
      <a title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.family}}" href="/freestyle/tricks?view=family">By family</a>
    {{/if}}
    <span class="trick-view-toggle-sep">·</span>
    {{#if (eq content.activeView "set")}}
      <span title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.set}}" class="trick-view-toggle-active">By set</span>
    {{else}}
      <a title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.set}}" href="/freestyle/tricks?view=set">By set</a>
    {{/if}}
    <span class="trick-view-toggle-sep">·</span>
    {{#if (eq content.activeView "modifier")}}
      <span title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.modifier}}" class="trick-view-toggle-active">By modifier</span>
    {{else}}
      <a title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.modifier}}" href="/freestyle/tricks?view=modifier">By modifier</a>
    {{/if}}
    {{! The specialist / analytical lenses stay reachable behind one disclosure
        so the prominent row carries only the curated first-class browse axes.
        Rendered open when the active view lives inside it, so the active entry
        is visible. }}
    <details class="trick-view-toggle-other"{{#if content.navSection.otherViewsOpen}} open{{/if}}>
      <summary>Other views</summary>
      <span class="trick-view-toggle-other-row">
        {{#if (eq content.activeView "movement-system")}}
          <span title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.movementSystem}}" class="trick-view-toggle-active">By movement system</span>
        {{else}}
          <a title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.movementSystem}}" href="/freestyle/tricks?view=movement-system">By movement system</a>
        {{/if}}
        <span class="trick-view-toggle-sep">·</span>
        {{#if (eq content.activeView "topology")}}
          <span title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.topology}}" class="trick-view-toggle-active">Movement Neighborhoods</span>
        {{else}}
          <a title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.topology}}" href="/freestyle/tricks?view=topology">Movement Neighborhoods</a>
        {{/if}}
        <span class="trick-view-toggle-sep">·</span>
        {{#if (eq content.activeView "dex-count")}}
          <span title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.dexCount}}" class="trick-view-toggle-active">By dex count</span>
        {{else}}
          <a title="{{content.navSection.viewTitles.dexCount}}" href="/freestyle/tricks?view=dex-count">By dex count</a>
        {{/if}}
      </span>
    </details>
  </nav>
  {{! Reference surfaces that are NOT dictionary browse axes, so they never
      belong in the View row above. This carried the browse grid's two
      cross-links, which is why it now renders on every view rather than only
      the secondary ones. }}
  <p class="trick-view-toggle-aside">New to the dictionary? Start with <a href="#reading-the-dictionary">Reading the Dictionary</a> above, look up a term in the <a href="/freestyle/glossary">Glossary</a>, or read the <a href="/freestyle/concepts">Freestyle Concepts</a> chapters. For modifier and operator vocabulary, see the <a href="/freestyle/operators">Operators &amp; Modifiers reference</a> (not a dictionary browse axis; it's vocabulary that helps you read trick names). For set systems as first-class objects (what is pixie / stepping / atomic as a system?), see the <a href="/freestyle/sets">Set Encyclopedia</a>.</p>

  {{#if (eq content.activeView "add")}}
  {{! Within-tier browse mode: Alphabetical (default, flat A-Z for lookup) or
      By family (nearest-anchor family bands in public-family order). Selected
      via ?sort=; server-rendered, no JavaScript. }}
  <nav class="trick-view-toggle" aria-label="Sort within each ADD tier">
    <span class="dict-nav-label">{{content.navSection.sortLabel}}</span>
    {{#if (eq content.addSort "alpha")}}
      <a href="{{{content.addSortToggle.familyHref}}}">By family</a>
      <span class="trick-view-toggle-sep">·</span>
      <span class="trick-view-toggle-active">Alphabetical</span>
    {{else}}
      <span class="trick-view-toggle-active">By family</span>
      <span class="trick-view-toggle-sep">·</span>
      <a href="{{{content.addSortToggle.alphaHref}}}">Alphabetical</a>
    {{/if}}
  </nav>
  {{#if content.addJumpChips.length}}
  <nav class="jump-bar" aria-label="Browse by ADD level">
    <span class="jump-bar-label">ADD levels:</span>
    {{#each content.addJumpChips}}
      <a href="{{{href}}}">{{label}}</a>{{#unless @last}} <span class="jump-bar-sep">·</span> {{/unless}}
    {{/each}}
  </nav>
  {{/if}}
  {{/if}}
  </div>

  {{! ── Default ADD-grouped view — two-line row contract.
       Every row: line 1 = name/hashtag/≡interpretation/media; line 2 =
       JOB: + ADD:. No green ADD chip (the value is in the section header
       + the line-2 ADD: formula). See dictionary-trick-row.hbs. }}
  {{#if (eq content.activeView "add")}}
  {{#each content.addGroups}}
  <section class="content-section trick-add-group" id="{{anchorId}}">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>{{addLabel}}</h2>
      <span class="section-count">{{countLabel}}</span>
    </div>
    {{#if (eq @root.content.addSort "alpha")}}
    {{! Alphabetical: flat A-Z across the whole tier, by canonical name. }}
    <div class="dict-trick-row-stack">
      {{#each cards}}
        {{> dictionary-trick-row}}
      {{/each}}
    </div>
    {{else}}
    {{! By family: nearest-anchor family bands in public-family order; the
        "Other / standalone tricks" band trails, alphabetized. Family parents
        / minor lineages only — no surface/root buckets. }}
    {{#each lineageBands}}
    <div class="trick-add-lineage">
      <h3 class="add-lineage-header">{{rootLabel}}</h3>
      <div class="dict-trick-row-stack">
        {{#each cards}}
          {{> dictionary-trick-row}}
        {{/each}}
      </div>
    </div>
    {{/each}}
    {{/if}}
  </section>
  {{/each}}
  {{/if}}

  {{! ── Dex Count view — two-line row contract.
      Buckets active tricks by the number of [DEX] tokens in their operational
      notation. Same generalized dictionary-trick-row partial as the ADD and
      Family views; only the bucketing axis differs. }}
  {{#if (eq content.activeView "dex-count")}}
  {{#if content.dexCountIntro}}<p class="browse-view-intro">{{content.dexCountIntro}}</p>{{/if}}
  {{#if content.dexCountScale}}<p class="browse-view-scale">{{content.dexCountScale}}</p>{{/if}}
  {{! In-view jump nav (mirrors By ADD). Static hash anchors into each dex bucket. }}
  {{#if content.dexCountGroups.length}}
  <nav class="jump-bar" aria-label="Jump to dex bucket">
    <span class="jump-bar-label">Jump to:</span>
    {{#each content.dexCountGroups}}
